## 🛡 ENFORCEMENT MECHANISMS

These principles are enforced through four layers:

### Layer A — Database (most important)
- Naming convention: `*_anonymous` RPCs for Analytics Mode, `*_support` for Support Mode
- Support Mode RPCs MUST check `impersonation_audit` has a non-expired `support_mode_enter` entry for the calling user
- Code review checklist verifies no PII columns in `*_anonymous` return shapes

### Layer B — Service / API
- `admin-command.service.ts` MUST split into:
  - `admin-analytics.service.ts` (Privacy-Safe)
  - `admin-support.service.ts` (PII, requires Support Mode token)
- Support service functions MUST receive an `auditId` parameter, passed to every RPC for traceability

### Layer C — UI / UX
- `CommandCenterOverview.tsx` calls Analytics service ONLY (no PII visible)
- A separate `SupportConsole.tsx` (future) handles Support Mode UI
- The "View as" button is moved from QuickSearchPalette to SupportConsole (requires Support Mode first)
- The QuickSearchPalette in Analytics Mode searches against anonymous aggregates (e.g., "orgs with >100 tx") not by name

### Layer D — Audit
- `impersonation_audit` is the source of truth for who-saw-what-when
- Compliance review process: monthly extract of all `support_mode_enter` events with reasons
- If a Support Mode session has no `query_metadata.reason` longer than 20 chars, deployment FAILS pre-prod tests

