## 📖 RATIONALE

Why this matters for LedgiProof specifically:

1. **Bookkeeper trust**: Professional bookkeepers handle attorney-client analog data. Knowing the SuperAdmin CANNOT browse their client list at will is a sales differentiator vs QuickBooks.

2. **Regulatory positioning**: SOC 2 Type II requires Principle of Least Privilege. "Admin sees everything always" fails the control. Privacy-Safe Analytics by default + audited Support Mode satisfies the control.

3. **Insider threat reduction**: Bad actors with admin credentials can extract competitive intelligence (e.g., "which restaurants in NYC use LedgiProof and have $X revenue?"). Aggregate-only default makes this impossible. Support Mode requires a reason that creates evidence.

4. **Compliance reporting**: When auditors ask "show us all PII access events in Q4", LedgiProof can produce the query above. Most SaaS platforms cannot.

5. **Customer ROIs**: AL plans to position LedgiProof as audit-grade. The CGC Core hash chain + Privacy-Safe Admin combine into a compelling "we cannot read your books without your knowledge" story.

6. **AI safety future-proofing**: When AI features are added (Customer Service IA, Schedule C explanations), they CANNOT have routine access to PII. Same principle: AI gets aggregates; user-specific context only via Support Mode equivalent.

