## 🚦 RELATIONSHIP TO ADDENDUM #1 (CHAT GOVERNANCE)

Addendum #2 is layered ON TOP OF Addendum #1:

| Concept | Addendum #1 (Chat) | Addendum #2 (Analytics) |
|---|---|---|
| What's protected | Communication content | Operational metadata + identities |
| Mechanism | Channel isolation + RLS structural rejection | Aggregate-only RPCs + explicit mode switch |
| SuperAdmin baseline access | Zero (rejected by RLS) | Aggregates only (no PII) |
| Elevation possible? | NO — workspace chats are NEVER accessible to admin | YES — Support Mode unlocks PII for time-boxed window |
| Trigger | User-initiated tickets only | Admin self-elevation with reason |

Together they form a defense-in-depth privacy architecture:
- **Chat content**: protected by Addendum #1 (structural, no escape hatch)
- **Identity/Metadata**: protected by Addendum #2 (default-deny, time-boxed elevation with audit)

